    {
      "v": 8,
      "zh": "现在耶和华―我们的　神暂且施恩与我们，给我们留些逃脱的人，使我们安稳如钉子钉在他的圣所，我们的　神好光照我们的眼目，使我们在受辖制之中稍微复兴。",
      "en": "“But now briefly[NOTE:1] we have received mercy from the Lord our God, in that he has left us a remnant and has given us a secure position[NOTE:2] in his holy place. Thus our God has enlightened our eyes[NOTE:3] and has given us a little relief in our time of servitude.",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “according to a little moment.”",
        "Heb “a peg” or “tent peg.” The imagery behind this word is drawn from the experience of nomads who put down pegs as they pitched their tents and made camp after times of travel.",
        "Heb “to cause our eyes to shine.” The expression is a figure of speech for “to revive.” See DCH 1:160 s.v. אור Hi.7."
      ],
